44qg848hwt8d"/><owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Augustine_of_Hippo"/></edm:Agent><ore:Aggregation rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"><edm:aggregatedCHO rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"/><edm:dataProvider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004502183"></edm:dataProvider><edm:isShownAt rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/sl/0001"/><edm:isShownBy rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/bnf/bnf-lat11641/bnf-lat11641_008v.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:object rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/loris/bnf/bnf-lat11641/bnf-lat11641_008v.jp2/full/full/0/default.jpg"/><edm:provider rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/organization/1482250000004671163"></edm:provider><edm:rights rdf:resource="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/"/></ore:Aggregation><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/provider/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"><dc:coverage>Lyon or Luxeuil</dc:coverage><dc:creator>Augustinus, Aurelius</dc:creator><dc:date>7th / 8th century</dc:date><dc:description>"Codex Florus dispersus” contains a virtual reconstruction of a manuscript of letters and sermons by Augustine. It was written by a single hand in a late 7th or early 8th century uncial script. The manuscript evidently originated in France, perhaps in Luxeuil or in Lyon. Originally the manuscript contained at least 30 quinions (at least 300 leaves), of which 117 leaves remain today. One part with 63 leaves from the original quires 4-11 is currently held in Paris (BnF, lat. 11641); after leaf 26 there could be inserted a single leaf which currently is held in St. Petersburg (NLR, Lat.F.papyr. I.1). Another part with 53 leaves from the original quires 24-30 is being held in Geneva (Bibliothèque de Genève, lat. 16). The outer leaf of each quire (quinio) is parchment, while the remaining leaves are papyrus. During the 9th century the volume was part of the library of Florus of Lyon, who added numerous marginalia to the manuscript in his own hand. "sine loco", codices restituti, Cod. 1 contains a virtual reconstruction of the surviving pieces in their original order.</dc:description><dc:format>117 ff., 32 x 22 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-sl-0001</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/sl/0001</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>[sine loco], codices restituti, Cod. 1 (Codex Florus dispersus)</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>Latin</dc:language><dc:rights>e-codices / [sine loco], codices restituti (cf. http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/about/terms)</dc:rights><dc:source rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/sl/0001"></dc:source><dc:title>[sine loco], codices restituti, Cod. 1 (Codex Florus dispersus) : Augustinus Hipponensis, Epistolae et Sermones  (Codex restitutus)</dc:title><dc:type>Virtual manuscript</dc:type><dcterms:medium>Papyrus and parchment</dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><ore:Proxy rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/proxy/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"><dc:creator rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/agent/171259"></dc:creator><edm:europeanaProxy>true</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"/><edm:type>TEXT</edm:type></ore:Proxy><edm:EuropeanaAggregation rdf:about="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/europeana/9200211/en_list_one_sl_0001"><edm:aggregatedCHO rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/920